summary:
  A rebuild that reloads a Bluetooth loopback with unchanged lags goes back
  to keeping the drift history and letting the first probe after it count,
  so the transport's re-roll is filed as drift.

history:
  Seen live on the work machine 2026-08-13. The room parked at 05:35,
  woke at 07:16:31 with the same lags it slept with, and the drift
  bookkeeping was left untouched because the schedule had not changed.
  The first probe after the wake read 47 ms; the settle tick 104 s later
  read 8. The 47 was a Bluetooth buffer that had just been re-rolled by
  the reload, and it went into the fold's history as if the room had
  drifted. The reset was gated on blChanged since 2026-08-02 under the
  rule "same lags out, same room after", which is true of a wired group
  and false whenever a bluez loopback goes out. This mutant puts that
  gate back.

target:
  package/contents/ui/SyncEngine.qml

find:
          if (blChanged || btReroll) {

replace:
          if (blChanged) {

expect:
  Killed by tests/qml/tst_syncengine.qml
  test_a_rebuild_with_a_bluetooth_member_spends_the_next_probe_even_when_nothing_changed
  and test_the_build_itself_arms_the_spend_for_a_bluetooth_group.
  Line-neutral.
